    "created_at": "2015-10-08T22:44:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-08T22:44:26Z",
    "body": "> I just wondered if it should be listed as a deliberate violation of the Unicode Standard.\n\nIt’s not at all clear that it violates any normative requirement in the Unicode Standard. It’s not clear that the Unicode Standard normatively states any relevant requirement. From the fact that it includes _LS_ and  _PS_ as line separators, it does not necessarily follow that there’s any normative requirements related to them for processing apps.\n",
